  "Content": {
    "Html": "<p>A signed bookplate makes a great keepsake for any of your copies of <em>How Not to Diet</em>, <em>How Not to Die</em>, or either of my cookbooks (see them all <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/books/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">here</a>). Donate any amount using <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.z2systems.com/np/clients/nutritionfacts/donation.jsp?campaign=58&amp;&amp;test=true\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" data-cke-saved-href=\"https://nutritionfacts.z2systems.com/np/clients/nutritionfacts/donation.jsp?campaign=58&amp;&amp;test=true\">this form</a> and we will send you a bookplate signed by me as a thank you gift. All proceeds go to keeping NutritionFacts.org growing and going! Donate today as this form will only be open while supplies last.</p>\n<h4 class=\"null\"><em>How Not to Diet</em> Out Now in Spanish </h4>\n<p><em><img decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignleft wp-image-67357 size-large\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/04/Full-Group–Out-Now-1024x1024.jpg\" alt=\"Spanish How Not to Diet\" width=\"200\" height=\"200\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/04/Full-Group–Out-Now-1024x1024.jpg 1024w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/04/Full-Group–Out-Now-960x960.jpg 960w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/04/Full-Group–Out-Now-768x768.jpg 768w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/04/Full-Group–Out-Now-500x500.jpg 500w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/04/Full-Group–Out-Now.jpg 1200w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/04/Full-Group–Out-Now-720x720.jpg 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/04/Full-Group–Out-Now-540x540.jpg 540w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 200px) 100vw, 200px\"/>How Not to Diet</em> is now available in Spanish in hardcover and ebook editions on <a href=\"https://www.amazon.es/Comer-para-engordar-innovadora-Divulgaci%C3%B3n/dp/8449338085/ref=sr_1_3?__mk_es_ES=%C3%85M%C3%85%C5%BD%C3%95%C3%91&amp;dchild=1&amp;keywords=comer+para+no+engordar&amp;qid=1615370232&amp;sr=8-3\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" data-cke-saved-href=\"https://www.amazon.es/Comer-para-engordar-innovadora-Divulgaci%C3%B3n/dp/8449338085/ref=sr_1_3?__mk_es_ES=%C3%85M%C3%85%C5%BD%C3%95%C3%91&amp;dchild=1&amp;keywords=comer+para+no+engordar&amp;qid=1615370232&amp;sr=8-3\">Amazon.es</a>, <a href=\"https://www.amazon.com.mx/Comer-para-engordar-innovadora-permanente-ebook/dp/B08YDNCRT2/ref=sr_1_1?__mk_es_MX=%C3%85M%C3%85%C5%BD%C3%95%C3%91&amp;dchild=1&amp;keywords=comer+para+no+engordar&amp;qid=1615370260&amp;sr=8-1\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" data-cke-saved-href=\"https://www.amazon.com.mx/Comer-para-engordar-innovadora-permanente-ebook/dp/B08YDNCRT2/ref=sr_1_1?__mk_es_MX=%C3%85M%C3%85%C5%BD%C3%95%C3%91&amp;dchild=1&amp;keywords=comer+para+no+engordar&amp;qid=1615370260&amp;sr=8-1\">Amazon.com.mx</a>, and other online retailers. More information and the links for several stores can be found <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/es/libro/comer-para-no-engordar/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" data-cke-saved-href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/es/comer-para-no-engordar/\">here</a>. You can find the availability of all translations of all of my books <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.zendesk.com/hc/en-us/articles/209667398-How-to-order-the-books-in-another-country\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" data-cke-saved-href=\"https://nutritionfacts.zendesk.com/hc/en-us/articles/209667398-How-to-order-the-books-in-another-country\">here</a>. </p>\n<p>And, if you prefer to get our newsletter in Spanish, just <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/es/suscribete/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">sign up here</a>. </p>\n<h4> </h4>\n<h4> </h4>\n<h4> </h4>\n<h4 class=\"null\">Key Takeaways: Environment</h4>\n<p data-pm-slice=\"1 1 []\"><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/topics/environment/\"><img decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignleft wp-image-67355 size-large\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/04/Environment-Square-1024x1024.jpg\" alt=\"Environment. Sea and sandy beach\" width=\"200\" height=\"200\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/04/Environment-Square-1024x1024.jpg 1024w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/04/Environment-Square-960x960.jpg 960w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/04/Environment-Square-768x768.jpg 768w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/04/Environment-Square-500x500.jpg 500w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/04/Environment-Square-1200x1200.jpg 1200w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/04/Environment-Square-720x720.jpg 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/04/Environment-Square-540x540.jpg 540w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/04/Environment-Square.jpg 1280w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 200px) 100vw, 200px\"/></a>In honor of Earth Day, we are highlighting the relationship between what we eat and the environment this month. What role does our food play in climate change? Which diet has the least impact on the environment? Check out the <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/topics/environment/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">topic page</a> for information from microplastics to foods with the lowest carbon footprint. </p>\n<p><em>“Simply cutting down on the meat you eat to less than an ounce or two a day can dramatically reduce greenhouse gas emissions. In terms of land use, a more healthful diet, like a Mediterranean diet, may decrease your footprint by about a quarter, whereas even more plant-based diets can drop it by 50 percent or more.” </em>(From <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/which-diets-have-the-lowest-carbon-footprint/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Which Diets Have the Lowest Carbon Footprint?</a>)</p>\n<p data-pm-slice=\"1 1 []\"> </p>\n<h4 class=\"null\">Recipe: Stuffed Sweet Potatoes with Balsamic Date Glaze</h4>\n<p><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/recipe/stuffed-sweet-potatoes-with-balsamic-date-glaze/\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignleft wp-image-67361 size-large\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/04/SSP-Recipe-1024x1024.jpg\" alt=\"Stuffed Sweet Potatoes\" width=\"200\" height=\"200\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/04/SSP-Recipe-1024x1024.jpg 1024w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/04/SSP-Recipe-960x960.jpg 960w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/04/SSP-Recipe-768x768.jpg 768w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/04/SSP-Recipe-500x500.jpg 500w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/04/SSP-Recipe-1200x1200.jpg 1200w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/04/SSP-Recipe-720x720.jpg 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/04/SSP-Recipe-540x540.jpg 540w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/04/SSP-Recipe.jpg 2000w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 200px) 100vw, 200px\"/></a>I love sweet potatoes. They’re one of the healthiest foods on the planet and one of the tastiest, too. The purple ones are the best, and you can usually find them at Asian markets and specialty natural groceries. They’re so good and good for you that I usually send them out in the mail as holiday gifts! Get the recipe <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/recipe/stuffed-sweet-potatoes-with-balsamic-date-glaze/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">here</a>, and watch how it’s made on our <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/reel/CNVZD_aJKpn/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" data-cke-saved-href=\"https://www.instagram.com/reel/CNVZD_aJKpn/\">Reels</a> video.</p>\n<p> </p>\n<p> </p>\n<h4 class=\"null\">Welcome, Tabitha!</h4>\n<p data-pm-slice=\"1 1 []\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignleft wp-image-67307\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/04/Tabitha.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"200\" height=\"200\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/04/Tabitha.jpg 694w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/04/Tabitha-500x500.jpg 500w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/04/Tabitha-540x540.jpg 540w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 200px) 100vw, 200px\"/>Tabitha joins us as our new Digital Outreach Assistant. With a business administration degree from Western Michigan University and an extensive marketing background, Tabitha works with our Digital Outreach Director to optimize and execute <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/\">NutritionFacts.org</a>’s digital marketing campaigns and improve our SEO strategies. She balances these analytical projects with creative hobbies such as photography, reading, and writing. Originally from Michigan, Tabitha now lives in Atlanta where she enjoys hiking, golfing, and racquetball. </p>\n<p data-pm-slice=\"1 1 []\"> </p>\n<h4 data-pm-slice=\"1 1 []\">Volunteer Spotlight: Patricia Penna</h4>\n<p data-pm-slice=\"1 1 []\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignleft\" src=\"https://mcusercontent.com/c1bae6687e1e6ab175fb56913/_compresseds/c0851311-59bb-4f18-8047-60a35e3e2633.jpg\" width=\"201\" height=\"268\" align=\"left\" data-file-id=\"5722\" data-cke-saved-src=\"https://mcusercontent.com/c1bae6687e1e6ab175fb56913/_compresseds/c0851311-59bb-4f18-8047-60a35e3e2633.jpg\"/>I’ve been volunteering with NutritionFacts.org for almost four years. I started helping with video uploads and now help with <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/blog/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">blog uploads</a>. <a href=\"https://NutritionFacts.org/\">NutritionFacts.org</a>‘s mission, empowering people with evidence-based information on the benefits of a whole food, plant-based diet, is what inspires me to support their work and help spread the word. I am happy to know that I contribute a bit to their amazing work. </p>\n<p>Favorite Recipe: I love this <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/recipe-veggie-mac-cheese/\">Veggie Mac &amp; Cheese</a>. It has my favorite foods: pasta, kale, a creamy cashew sauce, herbs, spices and tomatoes. Super easy, delicious, and nutritious.</p>\n<p> </p>\n<p> </p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignnone wp-image-60211 size-large\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/08/Top-3-Videos-of-the-Month-1024x331.png\" alt=\"Top 3 Videos of the Month\" width=\"460\" height=\"149\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/08/Top-3-Videos-of-the-Month-1024x331.png 1024w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/08/Top-3-Videos-of-the-Month-960x310.png 960w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/08/Top-3-Videos-of-the-Month-768x248.png 768w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/08/Top-3-Videos-of-the-Month-720x233.png 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/08/Top-3-Videos-of-the-Month-540x174.png 540w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/08/Top-3-Videos-of-the-Month.png 1108w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 460px) 100vw, 460px\"/></p>\n<p> </p>\n<p><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/flashback-friday-the-best-diet-for-diabetes/\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignleft wp-image-66833\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/03/2-1024x576.jpg\" alt=\"Flashback Friday: The Best Diet for Diabetes\" width=\"251\" height=\"141\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/03/2-1024x576.jpg 1024w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/03/2-960x540.jpg 960w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/03/2-768x432.jpg 768w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/03/2-480x270.jpg 480w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/03/2-1200x675.jpg 1200w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/03/2-720x405.jpg 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/03/2-540x304.jpg 540w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/03/2.jpg 1920w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 251px) 100vw, 251px\"/></a><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/flashback-friday-the-best-diet-for-diabetes/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Flashback Friday: The Best Diet for Diabetes</a></p>\n<p>The case for using a plant-based diet to reduce the burden of diabetes has never been stronger.</p>\n<p> </p>\n<p> </p>\n<p><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/do-angioplasty-heart-stent-procedures-work/\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignleft wp-image-66624\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/01/53-5-Do-Angioplasty-Heart-Stent-Procedures-Work-1024x576.jpg\" alt=\"Do Angioplasty Heart Stent Procedures Work?\" width=\"249\" height=\"140\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/01/53-5-Do-Angioplasty-Heart-Stent-Procedures-Work-1024x576.jpg 1024w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/01/53-5-Do-Angioplasty-Heart-Stent-Procedures-Work-960x540.jpg 960w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/01/53-5-Do-Angioplasty-Heart-Stent-Procedures-Work-768x432.jpg 768w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/01/53-5-Do-Angioplasty-Heart-Stent-Procedures-Work-480x270.jpg 480w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/01/53-5-Do-Angioplasty-Heart-Stent-Procedures-Work-1200x675.jpg 1200w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/01/53-5-Do-Angioplasty-Heart-Stent-Procedures-Work-720x405.jpg 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/01/53-5-Do-Angioplasty-Heart-Stent-Procedures-Work-540x304.jpg 540w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/01/53-5-Do-Angioplasty-Heart-Stent-Procedures-Work.jpg 1920w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 249px) 100vw, 249px\"/></a><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/do-angioplasty-heart-stent-procedures-work/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Do Angioplasty Heart Stent Procedures Work?</a></p>\n<p>There are demonstrably no benefits to the hundreds of thousands of angioplasty and stent procedures performed outside of an emergency setting. They don’t prevent heart attacks, enable you to live longer, or even help with symptoms any more than placebo (fake) surgery.</p>\n<p> </p>\n<p><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/why-angioplasty-heart-stents-dont-work-better/\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignleft wp-image-66629\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/01/53-6-Why-Angioplasty-Heart-Stents-Don’t-Work-Better-1024x576.jpg\" alt=\"Why Angioplasty Heart Stents Don’t Work Better\" width=\"249\" height=\"140\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/01/53-6-Why-Angioplasty-Heart-Stents-Don’t-Work-Better-1024x576.jpg 1024w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/01/53-6-Why-Angioplasty-Heart-Stents-Don’t-Work-Better-960x540.jpg 960w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/01/53-6-Why-Angioplasty-Heart-Stents-Don’t-Work-Better-768x432.jpg 768w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/01/53-6-Why-Angioplasty-Heart-Stents-Don’t-Work-Better-480x270.jpg 480w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/01/53-6-Why-Angioplasty-Heart-Stents-Don’t-Work-Better-1200x675.jpg 1200w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/01/53-6-Why-Angioplasty-Heart-Stents-Don’t-Work-Better-720x405.jpg 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/01/53-6-Why-Angioplasty-Heart-Stents-Don’t-Work-Better-540x304.jpg 540w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/01/53-6-Why-Angioplasty-Heart-Stents-Don’t-Work-Better.jpg 1920w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 249px) 100vw, 249px\"/></a><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/why-angioplasty-heart-stents-dont-work-better/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Why Angioplasty Heart Stents Don’t Work Better</a></p>\n<p>Most heart attacks are caused by nonobstructive plaques that infiltrate the entire coronary artery tree. There is no such thing as “1-vessel disease,” “2-vessel disease,” or “left main disease.” Atherosclerotic plaque is continuous throughout the coronary arteries of heart attack victims.</p>\n<p> </p>\n<h4 class=\"null\">Next Live Q&amp;A…TODAY!</h4>\n<p>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignleft wp-image-53879 size-large\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2018/05/LiveQANewsletter-Square-1024x1024.png\" alt=\"Live Q&amp;A\" width=\"200\" height=\"200\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2018/05/LiveQANewsletter-Square-1024x1024.png 1024w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2018/05/LiveQANewsletter-Square-960x960.png 960w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2018/05/LiveQANewsletter-Square-768x768.png 768w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2018/05/LiveQANewsletter-Square-500x500.png 500w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2018/05/LiveQANewsletter-Square-1200x1200.png 1200w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2018/05/LiveQANewsletter-Square-720x720.png 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2018/05/LiveQANewsletter-Square-540x540.png 540w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2018/05/LiveQANewsletter-Square.png 2000w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 200px) 100vw, 200px\"/>Every month, I do a live Q&amp;A directly from my treadmill, and <em><strong>today, April 22</strong></em>, is the day.</p>\n<p>Join on our <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/NutritionFacts.org/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" data-cke-saved-href=\"https://www.facebook.com/NutritionFacts.org/\">Facebook</a> page or <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/c/NutritionfactsOrgMD/live\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" data-cke-saved-href=\"https://www.youtube.com/c/NutritionfactsOrgMD/live\">YouTube</a> channel at 3pm ET. I’ll be streaming to both at the same time.</p>\n<p>You can find links to past live Q&amp;As <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/live/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">here</a> on NutritionFacts.org. If that’s not enough, don’t forget I have an <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/audio/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">audio podcast</a> to keep you company, too.</p>\n<p>And we just joined TikTok! <a href=\"https://www.tiktok.com/@nutrition_facts_org\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" data-cke-saved-href=\"https://www.tiktok.com/@nutritionfacts_org?\">Give us a follow</a>!</p>\n<p>In health,<br/>\n<b>Michael Greger, M.D.</b></p>\n<p>PS: If you haven’t yet, you can subscribe to my free videos <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/subscribe/\"><b>here</b></a><b> </b>and watch my live, year-in-review presentations:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>2019: <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/evidence-based-weight-loss-live-presentation/\"><b>Evidence-Based Weight Loss</b></a></li>\n<li>2016: <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/how-not-to-die/\"><b>How Not To Die: The Role of Diet in Preventing, Arresting, and Reversing Our Top 15 Killers</b></a></li>\n<li>2015: <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/food-as-medicine/\"><b>Food as Medicine: Preventing and Treating the Most Dreaded Diseases with Diet</b></a></li>\n<li>2014: <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/from-table-to-able/\"><b>From Table to Able: Combating Disabling Diseases with Food</b></a></li>\n<li>2013: <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/more-than-an-apple-a-day-preventing-our-most-common-diseases/\"><b>More Than an Apple a Day</b></a></li>\n<li>2012: <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/uprooting-the-leading-causes-of-death/\"><b>Uprooting the Leading Causes of Death</b></a></li>\n</ul>"
